# lua(1)

## NAME

lua - the Lua interpreter

## SYNOPSIS

    lua [options] [script [args...]]

## DESCRIPTION

Runs Lua programs. Without a script, reads an interactive prompt (REPL) when standard input is a terminal, or runs standard input as a script otherwise.

There is no shell inside Lua: `os.execute`, `io.popen` and `os.tmpname` are not available.

The `peripheral` library uses the devices of the computer (peripheral(3)), and the `os` library has events, timers, time and power functions (os(3)). They follow the Lua APIs of CC: Tweaked.

## OPTIONS

- `-e stat`: execute the string
- `-i`: enter interactive mode after the script
- `-l name`: require the library
- `-v`: print version information
- `-E`: ignore environment variables
- `-`: run standard input

## SEE ALSO

peripheral(3), os(3), nano(1), sh(1)
